# Project repo layout

This file comes from the [copier-claude-project](https://github.com/avcopan/copier-claude-project)
template and is updated by `pixi run copier-update`.
Put project-specific instructions in `CLAUDE.md` instead.

## Layout

| path | Git repo? | what it holds |
|---|---|---|
| `~/proj/{{project_name}}/` (this repo) | yes | Context for Claude: instructions, notes, TODOs, plans, reference files, and `repos.txt` |
| `~/code/{{project_name}}/` | no | Just a parent folder for the code repos |
| `~/code/{{project_name}}/<repo>/` | yes | The code repositories being developed in this project, listed in `repos.txt` |

## Working with the code repos

- Code changes go in the code repos and are committed there, with `git -C ~/code/{{project_name}}/<repo> ...` or after `cd`-ing into the repo.
  Notes, TODOs, and plans go in this repo.
  Never commit files from one repo to another.
- Before working in a code repo, read its `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and `README.md`, if they exist.
  Claude Code does not load them automatically, since the code repos are outside this directory.
  Follow that repo's own conventions.
  The user decides when to push.
- Keep each code repo's `CLAUDE.md` standalone: it should only say things that hold for anyone who clones that repo on any machine.
  Facts about this workspace (where TODOs live, where sibling repos are cloned, how the repos relate to this project) go in this repo instead.
- If a repo listed in `repos.txt` is missing, ask the user to run `pixi run bootstrap`.
  `pixi run status` shows the state of each repo.
- To add a repo, clone it into `~/code/{{project_name}}/<name>`, add a `<name> <url> [branch] [upstream=<url>]` line to `repos.txt` (`upstream=` gives a fork's original repo, which bootstrap adds as the `upstream` remote), and remind the user to commit and push this repo.

## Planning documents

A project with a plan keeps these files in this repo.
The `project-plan` skill (`/project-plan`) creates them, migrates an older plan to this layout, writes step walkthroughs, and shows what is left to do.
This section applies once the project has a `PLAN.md`.

| file | what it holds |
|---|---|
| `PROMPT.md` | The seed prompt that the vision and plan are generated from: scope, responsibilities, and the resources to read. Deleted once the plan exists; `HISTORY.md` names the commit to recover it from |
| `VISION.md` | What is being built and why: architecture, principles, names, and a dated decision log |
| `PLAN.md` | Open and future work only. It starts with `## Now`, the steps currently open |
| `HISTORY.md` | Completed work, newest first: what was done, where, and how it differed from the plan |
| `walkthroughs/` | Detailed how-tos for `PLAN.md` steps that need one, named `YYYY-MM-DD-short-slug.md` (the date written) |

- When a step in `PLAN.md` is finished, remove it from `PLAN.md` and add it to `HISTORY.md` in the same commit.
  Never leave ticked boxes in `PLAN.md`.
  In `HISTORY.md`, say what now exists (repos, versions, branches) and, if the work went differently than planned, how and why.
- When the direction changes, update `VISION.md` first, then `PLAN.md`.
  Record each decision in the decision log of `VISION.md`, and link to it from `HISTORY.md` instead of repeating it.
- An open step links to its walkthrough.
  When the step is done, its `HISTORY.md` entry links to the walkthrough instead, and the file is kept.
  Walkthroughs are written to `walkthroughs/` (`/project-plan`), never kept only in Claude's plan file.
- Keep no separate `TODO.md`: small chores go under `## Now`.
- Edit `PLAN.md` in place.
  Don't regenerate it from the old prompt once work has started.

## This repo

- It is a Pixi workspace (`pixi.toml`), which can hold dependencies and tasks for running and testing the project's code.
- Template updates go through `pixi run copier-update` (see `~/proj/ref/cop/copier-pixi-templates.md`, section 3, for resolving conflicts).
  Never edit `.copier-answers.yml` by hand.
- The shared reference library is indexed at `~/proj/ref/INDEX.md`.
